# Copy to `.env.local` for local development. Never commit `.env.local`.
#
# There is exactly one variable. It is not a secret: the Render URL is public by
# nature, and every visitor's browser already has it. Nothing that reaches the
# browser should ever be secret — anything in this file is compiled into the JS
# bundle that ships to the client.
#
# Read in src/lib/api/config.ts, which is the only place in the frontend that
# touches process.env.

# The FastAPI backend. No trailing slash.
#
# Local:  http://localhost:8000
# Prod:   https://<your-service>.onrender.com
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ is required, not stylistic: Next.js inlines the value at BUILD
# time and replaces the literal `process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`. A dynamic
# lookup such as `process.env[name]` is NOT inlined and silently resolves to
# undefined, so config.ts writes it out literally and every other file uses the
# `API_BASE` it exports.
#
# Changing this on Vercel triggers a rebuild. That is what you want — a
# redeploy alone would ship a bundle still pointing at the old host.
#
# Leave it unset and the app runs on its typed fixtures, so `bun dev` works in a
# fresh checkout with no backend running.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000